 <p>A study schedule that works is one you can actually follow. To make a study schedule, start with the time you already have, give each subject a short, regular block, mix subjects instead of studying one subject all day, and build review into the same week — so you are revisiting material, not just meeting it once before an exam.</p>
 <p><b>Key takeaways:</b></p>
 <ul><li>Plan around the time you already have, not an ideal day you do not have.</li><li>Use short, regular study blocks rather than one very long session.</li><li>Mix subjects in a week so each one gets repeated contact.</li><li>Build review into the schedule, in the same week you first study the material.</li><li>Leave buffer time for missed sessions, so one busy day does not break the whole plan.</li></ul>
